    15	and further to a horizon-tail loss
    16	\[
    17	\Delta_T(H)=\sup_a\sum_{t\le T}\mathbb E[a\,1\{H<\tau_t(a)\le T-t\}].
    18	\]
    19	An even smaller truncation penalty is the comparator gap
    20	\[
    21	\Gamma_T(H)=\sup_a V_T(a)-\sup_a V_T^H(a)\le\Delta_T(H),
    22	\]
    23	which also suffices for the same reduction. However neither \(\gamma(h)\to0\), \(\Delta_T(H_T)=o(T)\), nor \(\Gamma_T(H_T)=o(T)\) is established as necessary; reports give counterexamples where long positive-payoff tails are sparse, predictable, or process-known.
