+A candidate abstraction is a prefix-compatibility gap \(\kappa\): can one common distribution over prefix quotes nearly attain the conditional expected prefix value for all indistinguishable continuations/horizons? On zero-block thresholds \(\{c_0,c_1\}\), \(\kappa=\alpha(c_0,c_1)\). This is only a lower-bound ingredient: transfer to regret needs the same prefix action law, a cap on outside/post-divergence learner surplus, and probability weighting for rare prefix events.
